WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:02.220
- Big investment banks and money managers

00:00:02.220 --> 00:00:04.920
didn't get much right in
their predictions for 2023.

00:00:04.920 --> 00:00:06.780
Most were betting on a recession,

00:00:06.780 --> 00:00:08.670
rate cuts from the federal reserve

00:00:08.670 --> 00:00:11.550
and a middling year from
the US stock market.

00:00:11.550 --> 00:00:15.480
Instead, the S&amp;P 500 gained nearly 25%.

00:00:15.480 --> 00:00:18.010
The Fed raised rates, and the US economy

00:00:18.010 --> 00:00:20.550
grew with the fastest pace in years.

00:00:20.550 --> 00:00:23.580
So what are the big
banks betting on in 2024?

00:00:23.580 --> 00:00:26.100
I'm gonna tell you what
Wall Street is predicting

00:00:26.100 --> 00:00:28.980
for the economy, what they're
expecting from the Fed,

00:00:28.980 --> 00:00:30.750
and how they're expecting the stock market

00:00:30.750 --> 00:00:32.310
to perform this year.

00:00:32.310 --> 00:00:33.210
Let's get into it.

00:00:35.416 --> 00:00:37.044
More than two-thirds of the economists

00:00:37.044 --> 00:00:39.900
at large financial institutions
that do business directly

00:00:39.900 --> 00:00:41.940
with the Fed said they expected the US

00:00:41.940 --> 00:00:43.800
to have a recession in 2023.

00:00:43.800 --> 00:00:45.960
We detailed a couple of
the recession predictions

00:00:45.960 --> 00:00:46.860
on this channel.

00:00:46.860 --> 00:00:48.960
Some analysts are saying
that the recession

00:00:48.960 --> 00:00:51.270
that most of Wall Street
predicted would hit this year

00:00:51.270 --> 00:00:52.740
hasn't been avoided.

00:00:52.740 --> 00:00:54.060
It's just been delayed.

00:00:54.060 --> 00:00:55.470
But it didn't happen.

00:00:55.470 --> 00:00:58.800
And in 2024, recession calls
are few and far between

00:00:58.800 --> 00:01:01.050
among economists and market forecasters.

00:01:01.050 --> 00:01:04.530
Most big banks expect the US
economy to grow by around 2%

00:01:04.530 --> 00:01:06.390
in line with its long-term trend.

00:01:06.390 --> 00:01:08.160
Citi is one of the few big banks

00:01:08.160 --> 00:01:09.720
predicting a recession this year,

00:01:09.720 --> 00:01:11.970
but even they aren't predicting
the stock market will fall.

00:01:11.970 --> 00:01:15.450
The bank is calling for
the S&amp;P 500 to end 2024

00:01:15.450 --> 00:01:18.900
just under 10% higher
than where it end in 2023.

00:01:18.900 --> 00:01:21.810
Deutsche Bank is also predicting
a US recession this year.

00:01:21.810 --> 00:01:22.980
The firm says the effects

00:01:22.980 --> 00:01:26.310
from the Fed's unprecedented
rate hiking cycle in 2023

00:01:26.310 --> 00:01:28.530
will bring about a mild
recession this year.

00:01:28.530 --> 00:01:30.407
But they're also predicting that US stocks

00:01:30.407 --> 00:01:32.753
rise by nearly 10%.

00:01:35.490 --> 00:01:37.470
Most big banks are predicting the Fed

00:01:37.470 --> 00:01:39.480
will be cutting interest rates this year.

00:01:39.480 --> 00:01:42.240
A few believe it's because
the US will have a recession,

00:01:42.240 --> 00:01:44.429
but most are predicting
that with inflation falling

00:01:44.429 --> 00:01:48.239
below 3% at the end of
2023, it will get close

00:01:48.239 --> 00:01:50.670
to the Fed's 2% target this year.

00:01:50.670 --> 00:01:52.890
And that will mean that
the US Central Bank

00:01:52.890 --> 00:01:55.500
can lower interest rates
to loosen up the economy.

00:01:55.500 --> 00:01:58.037
When the Fed cuts rates, it
is historically given a boost

00:01:58.037 --> 00:01:59.990
to stock and bond prices.

00:01:59.990 --> 00:02:01.980
That's expected to happen this year

00:02:01.980 --> 00:02:04.953
with most analysts predicting
positive stock returns.

00:02:07.170 --> 00:02:10.020
At the end of 2023, market
strategists predicted

00:02:10.020 --> 00:02:13.530
that the S&amp;P 500 would rise to 5,132.

00:02:13.530 --> 00:02:16.260
That's about 10% higher than
where the index closed the year

00:02:16.260 --> 00:02:17.610
according to FactSet.

00:02:17.610 --> 00:02:18.840
That was based on a collection

00:02:18.840 --> 00:02:21.314
of median target price
estimates for all the companies

00:02:21.314 --> 00:02:23.610
in the benchmark US stock index.

00:02:23.610 --> 00:02:26.970
The last survey of 2023 by
Bank of America Securities

00:02:26.970 --> 00:02:29.400
found that fund managers
were the most optimistic

00:02:29.400 --> 00:02:31.860
in any month since January, 2022,

00:02:31.860 --> 00:02:35.550
and the most bullish on
stocks since February, 2022.

00:02:35.550 --> 00:02:38.160
Some of the predictions
for the best market returns

00:02:38.160 --> 00:02:40.890
come from firms like Fundstrat
and Yardeni Research,

00:02:40.890 --> 00:02:44.130
which both called for the US
to avoid a recession last year.

00:02:44.130 --> 00:02:45.683
Some of the lowest market expectations

00:02:45.683 --> 00:02:48.450
come from J.P. Morgan and Morgan Stanley.

00:02:48.450 --> 00:02:52.260
J.P. Morgan sees a challenging
backdrop for markets overall

00:02:52.260 --> 00:02:54.060
and expects that companies will struggle

00:02:54.060 --> 00:02:55.890
to increase their profits significantly.

00:02:55.890 --> 00:02:58.200
And Morgan Stanley is
expecting an increase

00:02:58.200 --> 00:03:00.510
in the number of companies
defaulting on their loans.

00:03:00.510 --> 00:03:03.357
Big picture, most banks
see solid economic growth,

00:03:03.357 --> 00:03:06.432
lower inflation, and higher
stock prices this year,

00:03:06.432 --> 00:03:08.010
which sounds pretty good.

00:03:08.010 --> 00:03:11.176
But remember, big bank's
predictions for 2023

00:03:11.176 --> 00:03:13.290
didn't exactly pan out.

00:03:13.290 --> 00:03:14.283
So don't sleep.

